    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 139,
      "text": "Risk strata were derived in the development cohort and applied unchanged to the internal and external cohorts. Coverage denotes the proportion selected by each strategy, and event capture the proportion of all observed events within the selected group. Specificity denotes the proportion of non-event observations outside the selected group. External results are reported for 102 hospitalization episodes from 50 patients. Captured events are observed events, not events prevented by an intervention. Abbreviations: RBF-SVM, radial-basis-function support vector machine; CI, confidence interval.",
      "display_html": "Risk strata were derived in the development cohort and applied unchanged to the internal and external cohorts. Coverage denotes the proportion selected by each strategy, and event capture the proportion of all observed events within the selected group. Specificity denotes the proportion of non-event observations outside the selected group. External results are reported for 102 hospitalization episodes from 50 patients. Captured events are observed events, not events prevented by an intervention. Abbreviations: RBF-SVM, radial-basis-function support vector machine; CI, confidence interval."
